              <h3>How do I choose between contractor types?</h3>
              <p>For multi-trade projects, use a general contractor. For focused updates like cabinetry or flooring, a specialized contractor works well. For unique custom installations, look for custom carpentry experts. Design-build firms offer comprehensive solutions from design through completion.</p>

              <h3>What portfolio criteria should I evaluate?</h3>
              <p>Look for projects similar in scope, style, and complexity to yours. Verify the photos are genuinely theirs. Ask if you can visit a completed project in person — the best contractors welcome this.</p>

              <h3>What are the red flags to watch for?</h3>
              <p>Requesting 50%+ upfront, no license or insurance, inability to provide references, vague timelines and pricing, and high-pressure sales tactics are all reasons to walk away immediately.</p>

              <h3>Why hire a local Pennsylvania contractor?</h3>
              <p>Local contractors know Pennsylvania building codes, township permit requirements, and regional material suppliers. They have established relationships with inspectors and subcontractors, which means faster timelines and fewer compliance surprises.</p>
            </div>

